BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5293120c-3086-4223-a010-d9f00718219c@viewcy.olio
DTSTAMP:20260814T134641Z
DTSTART:20260818T233000Z
DTEND:20260819T010000Z
SUMMARY:Olio Read-in: Camus' The Myth of Sisyphus
DESCRIPTION:What gives your life meaning? What gets you out of bed each mor
 ning? What informs your choice to get up: obligations? Family? Coffee? Pur
 suit of Happiness? Sisyphus does not have the luxury of asking—or answer
 ing—these questions. Condemned by the gods to push a boulder up a mounta
 in\, only to watch it roll back down\, Sisyphus continues his journey: day
  in and day out\, up and down\, over and over—for eternity.Sisyphus' lot
  is terrible because it is eerily familiar. Day in and day out\, we snooze
  our alarms\, suffer the commute\, consume things we know aren't good for 
 us\, count down the hours until the workday ends\, scroll mindlessly\, and
  then do it all over again the next day. Why? If life is a routine that of
 fers no inherent meaning\; if the success\, progress\, and happiness we pu
 rsue are out of reach\, why get up? Why not end the ordeal? Why not deceiv
 e ourselves into believing that there is a higher purpose to our suffering
 s?&nbsp\;These are the questions Sisyphus invites us to confront.In this O
 lio Read-In\, Dina Odnopozova (PhD\, Yale\; Professor at Baruch College) w
 ill explore Albert Camus' “The Myth of Sisyphus” as a user’s manual 
 to life and an introduction to existentialist philosophy. Together\, we'll
  grapple with questions that are at once profoundly difficult and surprisi
 ngly simple: What makes life meaningful? How can we create meaning in the 
 meaningless world? And is it possible to be happy in the universe that is 
 indifferent to our predicaments?&nbsp\;Olio Read-ins were started by histo
 rian Jamie Warren:"Rooted in the social revolution of the 1960s\, Read-ins
  have always been essential to the political project of building communiti
 es\, and bolstering progressive change. Read-ins announce: We will not rem
 ain alone\, afraid\, and cut off from one another. No. We will sit side by
  side and with the support of each other\, we will read. We will learn. We
  will enrich our inner world so that we can find the courage to exist outs
 ide of it."Put simply by one of our Olio members: "Read-Ins are like the b
 ook club that I actually want to be a part of. It's so much more fun to en
 gage with these texts as a group and with a teacher than as a solo activit
 y." &nbsp\;Teacher: Dina Odnopozova Dina Odnopozova holds a PhD from Yale 
 and is a professor at Baruch College\, where her work explores the interse
 ction of literature\, psychology\, and the unconscious. She has led Olios 
 on Freud\, Jung\, and the archetypal grammar of fairy tales — the witche
 s\, wolves\, and forbidden doors that map the human subconscious. In this 
 Read-in\, she brings that same depth of attention to Camus.Think Olio is a
 n ongoing experiment in lifelong learning. We are a community of open-mind
 ed people who gather to exchange ideas with new friends and connect over a
 rt\, literature\, and philosophy. Check out our full calendar Our $30 memb
 ership gives you two events for the price of one!An Olio is what we call t
 he social learning events we've been organizing since 2015. A blend betwee
 n a lecture and a house party\, Olios are led by a teacher who loves shari
 ng their passions and the room is filled with curious\, open-minded New Yo
 rkers.Our goal is to spark new perspectives\, ignite curiosity\, and enjoy
  ourselves socially—an alternative to typical nightlife options.Disclaim
 er: By purchasing a ticket\, you agree to have your photo/video used for s
 ocial media/marketing materials. If you prefer to not have your photo take
 n\, feel free to send us a note. Photo by Zhi-Da Zhong\n\nTickets & info: 
 https://www.viewcy.com/event/olio_readin_camus
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/olio_readin_camus
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3833940b-0261-455e-9ca9-68f456a98af1@viewcy.olio
